      "spatial_support": "Mean of 30 m OpenET pixels inside each supplied field polygon; MultiPolygon parts are queried separately and area-weighted.",
      "limitations": "SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE: canned fake HTTP 200 responses passed through the adapter by prototype/fixtures/make_synthetic_et.py. Patterned test numbers, not OpenET values or measurements; retrieved_date is the fixture date. Must never enter the demo bundle. Modelled actual ET (ensemble mean of up to six satellite models after MAD outlier removal), not a measurement and not pumped irrigation: it includes water from rain, irrigation and shallow groundwater. High ET is not automatically crop stress; rain minus ET is only a partial water-balance indicator. The 200-response schema is undocumented; the parser accepts list-of-records JSON and saves raw responses. The OpenAPI spec lists no per-month quality-flag variable for this endpoint, so row quality only says reported/missing/area_weighted_from_parts. The product's own spread indicator is the ensemble MAD range (variables et_mad_min/et_mad_max, requested with --with-uncertainty)."
    }
